  "content": "National Women Team’s six members to play T20 in Malaysia\nOnlinekhabar\nFriday, October 10, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 10\nSix members of the National Women’s Cricket Team will be participating in the MCA Women’s T20 Inter-State Championship, scheduled to take place in Kuala Lumpur. The championship is being organised by the Malaysian Cricket Association from October 17 to 27.\nSita Rana Magar, Kabitra Joshi, Rajmati Airee, Rubina Chhetri, Puja Mahato, and Kabita Kunwar will be attending the event, said Cricket Association of Nepal (CAN) Spokesperson Chhumbi Lama.\nPrior to this, the Nepali Women’s Cricket Team had played in the Super Women Series held in Malaysia. During the series, Nepal played five T20 matches against the host and won the series 3-2.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nBP Highway\nFlowers\nnational women team\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nPolitics\nWho do student unions stand for? Questions rise after Gen Z Movement\n16 hours ago\nEconomy\nThai AirAsia to resume flights from Gautam Buddha International Airport\n16 hours ago\nFestival\nFlowers ready for Tihar Festival (Photos)\n16 hours ago\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n2 days ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n2 days ago",
